course: dictionary
lesson: 4481
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word harvest can be a verb or a noun, and it has more than one meaning. To harvest is to gather crops like corn, apples or wheat when they are ripe. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits.
explain: «Halloween on 31 October grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival at the end of the harvest.» Here the end of the harvest is a time of year, so harvest means the season when crops are gathered. In «a good harvest», the word means the amount of crops gathered.
explain: Use the swap check. Put your meaning in place of the word and read the sentence again. «Only the good soil gave a big harvest» still makes sense if you think of a big amount of crops, so that is the right meaning here.
fact: Harvest can be a verb (to harvest) or a noun (the harvest, a harvest).
fact: To harvest means to gather crops like corn, apples or wheat when they are ripe.
fact: The harvest can mean the time when crops are gathered, at the end of summer or in autumn.
fact: A harvest can also mean the amount of crops gathered, as in «a good harvest».
fact: «The harvest mouse is Britain's smallest rodent, about as heavy as a 20p coin.»
exercise: «Only the good soil gave a big harvest.» What does harvest mean here? | A storm at sea | To cut down trees | *The amount of crops gathered | A game played in the summer
exercise: A farmer gets 6 sacks of wheat from each acre of land. On 5 acres, what is the harvest? | 1 sack | *30 sacks | 11 sacks | 56 sacks
exercise: «Halloween grew from Samhain, an old Celtic festival at the end of the harvest.» What does harvest mean? | *The time when crops are gathered | Eating a big meal | A spooky costume
test: «Other faiths have harvest festivals too, such as the Jewish Sukkot and the Hindu Pongal.» What is a harvest festival? | A winter party with snow games | A race for farm animals | *A celebration linked to gathering crops
test: The harvest mouse is about as heavy as what? | A bag of sugar | A cup of tea | *A 20p coin | A school bus
exam: Which sentence uses harvest as a verb? | The harvest was late this year. | *Farmers harvest the wheat when it is ripe. | The harvest mouse is tiny. | We had a harvest festival at school.
